// spec: RT-002
//
// ⚠️ Expected to FAIL compiled, because of C-15: the emitter has no case for a
// call to a name it cannot resolve, so it refuses with 'A call to ''AssertTrue''
// is not supported by the C back end yet.' rather than letting the program run
// and fail on the undefined name.
// AssertTrue, AssertEqual and Fail are registered only while --test is
// running, so outside one the name is simply not there.

AssertTrue (True);
